+# @deepseek-ai/dsh-web-search-tavily
+
+English | [中文](README.zh.md)
+
+A [Tavily](https://tavily.com)-backed `WebSearchProvider` for the harness [web capability seam](../web/README.md) (`ctx.web`). It calls Tavily's `POST /search` endpoint and maps the generated `answer` plus the flat `results[]` into the seam's normalized `WebSearchResult`.
+
+This is an **implementation** package: it registers a provider into `ctx.web`, it does not own the `ctx.web` key and it does not register a model-facing tool (that is `@deepseek-ai/dsh-tool-web`). Like `@deepseek-ai/dsh-llm-deepseek`, it is a function/namespace plugin (`inject: ['web']`) that registers its backend, not a default-export service.
+
+## Config
+
+| Key | Default | Meaning |
+|---|---|---|
+| `apiKey` | `$TAVILY_API_KEY` | Tavily API key. Empty/absent makes the provider unavailable. |
+| `apiKeyEnv` | `TAVILY_API_KEY` | Environment variable naming the key when `apiKey` is absent. |
+| `baseURL` | `https://api.tavily.com` | Endpoint base; `/search` is appended. An unparseable value makes the provider unavailable. |
+| `maxResults` | (unset) | Default result count when a request carries no `maxResults`. Unset sends no default. Must be a positive integer. |
+| `searchDepth` | `basic` | Retrieval depth sent as Tavily's `search_depth`: `basic` (fast, lower cost) or `advanced` (deeper crawl). |
+
+```yaml
+- id: web-search-tavily
+  name: '@deepseek-ai/dsh-web-search-tavily'
+  config:
+    apiKeyEnv: TAVILY_API_KEY
+```
+
+## Mapping
+
+Every request sends `include_answer: true`, so Tavily generates an `answer` in addition to the flat `results[]`. The non-blank `answer` maps to `content`; each result maps to a `WebSearchSource`: `url` ← `url`, `title` ← `title`, `snippet` ← the non-blank `content` excerpt, `publishedAt` ← `publishedDate`. Absent, null, or empty optional fields are omitted rather than emitted, and a result without an excerpt still returns as a URL-only source. A request's `maxResults` wins over the configured default and is sent as Tavily's `max_results` for a cost/latency optimization; the final bound is enforced by the seam. Provider failures (HTTP errors, network failure, unparseable or wrong-shape bodies) surface as `WebError` `WEB_PROVIDER_ERROR`; an aborted request surfaces as `WEB_ABORTED`. HTTP redirects are rejected before the `Location` target is contacted and surface as `WEB_PROVIDER_ERROR`.
+
+## Model Experience
+
+### Web search tool results, indirectly
+
+#### What the model sees
+
+Through [`dsh-tool-web`](../tool-web/README.md), the conversation model sees the `maxResults`-bounded URLs, titles, excerpts, and publication dates plus the generated answer as `content`, or this provider's exact failures — `Tavily search aborted`, `Tavily search request failed: <error>`, the provider message on an HTTP error, and `Tavily returned an unprocessable response body: <error>` — under the consumer's error wrapper. Provider-private fields (scores, raw content) stay outside context.
+
+#### Token effect
+
+Zero direct conversation tokens from registration. Result tokens scale with the returned sources, answer, and snippets, then the seam enforces the requested source bound; the provider account is charged Tavily's per-search rate.
+
+#### KV Cache effect
+
+Append-only; newly visible content follows the reusable request prefix and does not invalidate existing KV-cache entries.
+
+## Known Limitations and Deferred Work
+
+- **`include_answer` is always on** — the generated answer costs Tavily-side latency and tokens on every search even when a consumer ignores `content`; there is no per-request answer toggle on the seam.
+- **Only `maxResults`/`searchDepth` are exposed** — Tavily's other controls (topic, days, include/exclude domains, raw content, answer length) wait on provider-neutral Service Definition fields ([seam Agent Note](../../../.agents/notes/implemented/architecture/2026-06-24-web-capability-seam.md)).
+- **Abort classification is error-shape-based** — only a `DOMException` named `AbortError` maps to `WEB_ABORTED`; an abort carrying a custom reason (e.g. `dsh-timeout`'s `TimeoutReason`) surfaces as `WEB_PROVIDER_ERROR`.
+- **Snippet and answer lengths are Tavily's own** — excerpts are Tavily's extracted text, not provider-neutral fields; a long excerpt is bounded only by the result-truncation budget of the seam.
